   "title": "Ripple and noise measurement set-up",
   "page": 5,
   "description": "The converter runs from a supply whose negative side is earthed, into a resistive load at its maximum rated power on twisted leads. C1 (ceramic) and C2 (tantalum) sit across the output; C3 and R1 in series feed a coax line, three turns of which pass through a ferrite toroid (T1), and R2 terminates the line at the oscilloscope's Y input. The coax screen joins the output return to the oscilloscope ground. The measured value is multiplied by 10.",
