 "equations": [],
 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Construction",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "The transformer is built into the circuit board, with FR4 as the insulation between its primary and secondary windings. The package is an inspectable iLGA on an industry-standard footprint."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Isolation testing",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "Every module is hi-pot tested at 3 kVDC for one second, and qualification samples for one minute. Used only as functional isolation, the barrier holds continuous or switched voltages up to 3 kV. Partial-discharge inception, measured to IEC 60270, was above 3.5 kV."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Repeated hi-pot",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "Repeated high-voltage testing can degrade the FR4 barrier, so repeat testing is advised against; where it is required, the test voltage is reduced by 20 %. The same applies to agency-rated parts, whose insulation is always supplemented by spacing or barriers."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Safety approvals",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "UL recognised (file E151252) to UL62368-1: reinforced insulation at 125 Vrms working and basic at 250 Vrms. Also recognised to ANSI/AAMI ES60601-1 for 1 MOOP at 250 Vrms max working between primary and secondary. Creepage and clearance 3 mm, altitude up to 5000 m, overvoltage category II."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Fusing",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "There is no fuse inside. For UL compliance a UL-recognised anti-surge fuse goes in the input line: 1 A on 5 V input models, 400 mA on 12 V input models, each rated for at least the highest DC input voltage."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Short circuit",
   "page": 6,
   "text": "The NXE2S0505MC is protected against an output short from -40 °C up to the temperatures in its short-circuit graph. The 12 V input models have momentary short-circuit protection only."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Minimum load",
   "page": 6,
   "text": "Specified performance needs at least 10 % of full load over the whole input range. Below 10 % the output voltage climbs, and with less than 5 % load it can reach about twice its nominal value."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Moisture",
   "page": 6,
   "text": "The module is not hermetic and must be dry before power is applied."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Output capacitance and start-up",
   "page": 6,
   "text": "Start-up times are given for a 2.2 µs input rise and 10 µF on the output. The modules will start into 47 µF with a longer start time, but 10 µF is the highest output capacitance recommended."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Output ripple filter parts",
   "page": 6,
   "text": "The filter capacitor wants the lowest ESR available, ceramic preferred, rated at least twice the output voltage (the 15 V model excepted). The inductor's current rating is no less than the module's output current, its DC drop at rated current stays under 2 % of the rated output voltage, and its self-resonance lies above 20 MHz."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Output tolerance",
   "page": 7,
   "text": "The tolerance envelope bounds the output voltage across load from 10 % to 100 % together with set-point error. The NXE2S1205MC and NXE2S1212MC move outside their envelopes at the ends of the operating temperature range."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Thermal",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "Cooling is by free air convection. The case runs 27 to 36 °C above ambient depending on model (32 °C for the NXE2S1205MC); each model's derating graph gives load against temperature."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Soldering",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "Suited to lead-free reflow and also to tin-lead. Classified to J-STD-020 at 260 °C peak, moisture sensitivity level 2; terminations are gold plated 0.12 µm thick."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Packing",
   "page": 12,
   "text": "Tape and reel to EIA-481: 180 parts on a 7 inch reel or 800 on a 13 inch reel, with at least 400 mm of leader (100 mm of it empty pockets minimum) and 160 mm of trailer."
  }
 ],
